<title>FRANCE: Euro-MPs approve EU law on vehicle safety tests.</title>
<headline>Euro-MPs approve EU law on vehicle safety tests.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Parliament approved on Thursday a draft directive on the approximation of member state laws on roadworthiness tests for motor vehicles and their trailers -- COM(95)415.</p>
<p>The deal involves the modification of a 1977 directive to include speed-limiting devices and tachographs on the list of points which have to be covered during annual vehicle checkups.</p>
<p>European Union transport ministers reached a provisional agreement on the proposal in June. It needed the approval of the Parliament to become law.</p>
</text>
